whisper: Hop! A small platformer. Left and right run, space jumps.
whisper: Pick up every coin, keep away from the spikes and the bees, then touch the flag at the far end.

use: window
use: maths
use: records.fathom

a platform has:
  x (a number)
  y (a number)
  width (a number)
  height (a number)
and the universe said i love you

a coin has:
  birth (a flat place)
and the universe said i love you

a spike has:
  x (a number)
  width (a number)
and the universe said i love you

a bee has:
  birth (a flat place)
  reach (a number)
and the universe said i love you

a queen bee is a kind of bee that has:
  crown (text)
and the universe said i love you

a danger is anything that can hurt and appear.

a trail of anything has:
  items (a list of anything)
and the universe said i love you

the world remembers:
  player x (a number)
  player y (a number)
  speed x (a number)
  speed y (a number)
  on ground (yes or no)
  facing (a number)
  platforms (a list of platforms)
  coins (a list of coins)
  coins taken (a number)
  spikes (a list of spikes)
  bees (a list of bees)
  queen (a queen bee)
  dust (a trail of flat places)
  palette (a table of text)
  score (a number)
  lives (a number)
  camera (a number)
  ticks (a number)
  seconds (a number)
  points (a number)
  won (yes or no)
  blink (yes or no)
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- making the level

to platform at, given x (a number) and y (a number) and width (a number) and height (a number), returning a platform:
  conjure a platform as made
  set the x of made to x
  set the y of made to y
  set the width of made to width
  set the height of made to height
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to coin at, given x (a number) and y (a number), returning a coin:
  conjure a coin as made
  set the birth of made to x horizontal y vertical
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to spike at, given x (a number) and width (a number), returning a spike:
  conjure a spike as made
  set the x of made to x
  set the width of made to width
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to build the level:
  add platform at with (0, 460, 760, 80) to platforms
  add platform at with (880, 460, 720, 80) to platforms
  add platform at with (1720, 460, 300, 80) to platforms
  add platform at with (2160, 460, 1040, 80) to platforms
  add platform at with (330, 360, 160, 24) to platforms
  add platform at with (1180, 340, 140, 24) to platforms
  add platform at with (1400, 250, 140, 24) to platforms
  add platform at with (1840, 330, 120, 24) to platforms
  add platform at with (2400, 380, 60, 80) to platforms
  add platform at with (2640, 330, 60, 130) to platforms
  add coin at with (410, 320) to coins
  add coin at with (820, 380) to coins
  add coin at with (1250, 300) to coins
  add coin at with (1470, 210) to coins
  add coin at with (1900, 290) to coins
  add coin at with (2430, 340) to coins
  add coin at with (2670, 290) to coins
  add spike at with (1490, 72) to spikes
  add spike at with (1990, 24) to spikes
  conjure a bee as worker
  set the birth of worker to 1600 horizontal 120 vertical
  set the reach of worker to 60
  add worker to bees
  set the birth of queen to 2920 horizontal 190 vertical
  set the reach of queen to 70
  set the crown of queen to "#ffd54f"
and the universe said i love you

to choose the colours:
  set the entry "sky" of palette to "#8fd3ff"
  set the entry "hills" of palette to "#7fc8a9"
  set the entry "earth" of palette to "#8a5a33"
  set the entry "grass" of palette to "#4caf50"
  set the entry "gold" of palette to "#ffc107"
  set the entry "ink" of palette to "#1b2a49"
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- moving the player: speed changes the place, gravity changes the speed

to run and jump:
  if key held "left":
    set speed x to speed x minus 0.8
    set facing to -1
  otherwise if key held "right":
    set speed x to speed x plus 0.8
    set facing to 1
  otherwise:
    set speed x to speed x times 0.8
  set speed x to clamp speed x between -6 and 6
  if key pressed "space" and on ground:
    set speed y to -13
  set speed y to smaller of (speed y plus 0.6) and 14
and the universe said i love you

to overlaps, given p (a platform), returning yes or no:
  return player x plus 30 exceeds the x of p and player x falls below the x of p plus the width of p and player y plus 40 exceeds the y of p and player y falls below the y of p plus the height of p
and the universe said i love you

to test overlapping:
  set player x to 100
  set player y to 430
  check overlaps with platform at with (0, 460, 760, 80)
  set player y to 380
  check not overlaps with platform at with (0, 460, 760, 80)
and the universe said i love you

to move across:
  set player x to player x plus speed x
  for each p in platforms:
    if overlaps with p:
      if speed x exceeds 0: set player x to the x of p minus 30
      otherwise: set player x to the x of p plus the width of p
      set speed x to 0
  set player x to clamp player x between 0 and 3170
and the universe said i love you

to move up and down:
  set on ground to no
  set player y to player y plus speed y
  for each p in platforms:
    if overlaps with p:
      if speed y exceeds 0:
        set player y to the y of p minus 40
        set on ground to yes
      otherwise:
        set player y to the y of p plus the height of p
      set speed y to 0
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- coins: which ones are taken is kept in the bits of one number

to is taken, given n (a number), returning yes or no:
  return ((coins taken shifted right by (n minus 1)) bitwise and 1) is 1
and the universe said i love you

to pick up coins:
  set middle to (player x plus 15) horizontal (player y plus 20) vertical
  for each n from 1 to the size of coins:
    if not is taken with n and the existence of item n of coins is within 30 of middle:
      set coins taken to coins taken bitwise or (1 shifted left by (n minus 1))
      set score to score plus 1
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- dangers: spikes and bees are different kinds of things, but both can hurt and appear

to hurt, for a spike, returning yes or no:
  return player x plus 30 exceeds x and player x falls below x plus width and player y plus 40 exceeds 440
and the universe said i love you

to appear, for a spike:
  set left to x minus camera
  for each k from 0 to width divided by 12 minus 1:
    etch a box with left plus k times 12 plus 3, 446, 6, 14, "#90a4ae"
    etch a box with left plus k times 12 plus 5, 440, 2, 6, "#cfd8dc"
and the universe said i love you

to hurt, for a bee, returning yes or no:
  return existence is within 26 of (player x plus 15) horizontal (player y plus 20) vertical
and the universe said i love you

to appear, for a bee:
  set spot to existence minus camera horizontal 0 vertical
  etch a circle with spot of horizontal, spot of vertical, 12, "#fdd835"
  etch a box with spot of horizontal minus 4, spot of vertical minus 12, 3, 24, "#212121"
  etch a box with spot of horizontal plus 3, spot of vertical minus 12, 3, 24, "#212121"
  set flap to 4 plus 3 times sine of (ticks times 2000)
  etch a circle with spot of horizontal, spot of vertical minus 12 minus flap, 7, "#e3f2fd"
and the universe said i love you

to appear, for a queen bee:
  set spot to existence minus camera horizontal 0 vertical
  etch a circle with spot of horizontal, spot of vertical, 16, "#fbc02d"
  etch a box with spot of horizontal minus 5, spot of vertical minus 16, 4, 32, "#212121"
  etch a box with spot of horizontal plus 3, spot of vertical minus 16, 4, 32, "#212121"
  etch a box with spot of horizontal minus 9, spot of vertical minus 30, 18, 8, crown
and the universe said i love you

to fly, for a bee, given t (a number):
  set existence to birth plus (sine of (t times 90) times reach) horizontal (sine of (t times 240) times 10) vertical
and the universe said i love you

to the dangers, returning a list of dangers:
  set all to a list of dangers
  for each s in spikes: add s to all
  for each b in bees: add b to all
  add queen to all
  return all
and the universe said i love you

to the danger touching, returning a danger:
  for each d in the dangers:
    if hurt d: return d
  return no danger
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- starting again, and losing a life

to start again:
  set player x to 60
  set player y to 400
  set speed x to 0
  set speed y to 0
and the universe said i love you

to lose a life:
  set lives to lives minus 1
  if lives is 0:
    set lives to 3
    set score to 0
    set coins taken to 0
    set seconds to 0
  start again
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- the dust the player kicks up: a trail keeps the last few places

to leave, for a trail of anything, given x (anything):
  add x to items
  if the size of items exceeds 10: remove item 1 from items
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- drawing: the camera follows the player, and everything is etched where the camera sees it

to etch the sky:
  consume the window with the entry "sky" of palette
  for each n from 0 to 6:
    set hill x to n times 520 minus remainder of (camera times 0.3, 520)
    etch a circle with hill x, 560, 260, the entry "hills" of palette
  for each n from 0 to 8:
    set cloud x to n times 400 minus remainder of (camera times 0.15, 400)
    etch a circle with cloud x, 90 plus (remainder of (n, 3)) times 25, 26, "white"
    etch a circle with cloud x plus 30, 80 plus (remainder of (n, 3)) times 25, 32, "white"
    etch a circle with cloud x plus 62, 92 plus (remainder of (n, 3)) times 25, 24, "white"
and the universe said i love you

to etch the level:
  for each p in platforms:
    set left to the x of p minus camera
    etch a box with left, the y of p, the width of p, the height of p, the entry "earth" of palette
    etch a box with left, the y of p, the width of p, 10, the entry "grass" of palette
  for each n from 1 to the size of coins:
    if not is taken with n:
      set c to item n of coins
      set bob to sine of (ticks times 4 plus (the existence of c of horizontal)) times 4
      etch a circle with (the existence of c of horizontal) minus camera, (the existence of c of vertical) plus bob, 11, the entry "gold" of palette
      etch a circle with (the existence of c of horizontal) minus camera minus 3, (the existence of c of vertical) plus bob minus 3, 4, "#fff3c4"
  etch a box with 3060 minus camera, 300, 6, 160, "#5d4037"
  set flag colour to "#e53935"
  if score is the size of coins:
    set flag colour to "#43a047"
    if blink: set flag colour to "#a5d6a7"
  etch a box with 3066 minus camera, 300, 46, 30, flag colour
and the universe said i love you

to etch the dangers:
  for each d in the dangers: appear d
and the universe said i love you

to etch the player:
  for each spot in the items of dust:
    etch a circle with spot of horizontal minus camera, spot of vertical, 3, "#d7ccc8"
  set left to player x minus camera
  set squash to 0
  if not on ground: set squash to 4
  depending on lives:
    3: set body colour to "#3f51b5"
    2: set body colour to "#7e57c2"
    anything else: set body colour to "#e53935"
  etch a box with left, player y plus squash, 30, 40 minus squash, body colour
  set eye x to left plus 15 plus facing times 6
  etch a circle with eye x minus 5, player y plus 14, 4, "white"
  etch a circle with eye x plus 5, player y plus 14, 4, "white"
  etch a circle with eye x minus 5 plus facing, player y plus 14, 2, "black"
  etch a circle with eye x plus 5 plus facing, player y plus 14, 2, "black"
and the universe said i love you

to etch a heart, given x (a number) and y (a number) and size (a number, usually 9):
  etch a circle with x minus size divided by 2, y, size divided by 2 plus 1, "#e53935"
  etch a circle with x plus size divided by 2, y, size divided by 2 plus 1, "#e53935"
  etch a box with x minus size, y, size times 2, size divided by 2, "#e53935"
  etch a circle with x, y plus size, size divided by 2, "#e53935"
and the universe said i love you

to etch the score:
  set the text size to 26
  etch words with "Coins: [score] of [the size of coins]   Time: [seconds rounded to 1 decimal place]", 22, 18, the entry "ink" of palette
  set heart x to 900
  repeat lives times:
    etch a heart with heart x, 34
    set heart x to heart x minus 30
  if best time exceeds 0:
    set the text size to 18
    etch words with "Best: [best time rounded to 1 decimal place]   Points ever: [points ever]", 22, 52, the entry "ink" of palette
  if won:
    set the text size to 64
    etch words with "You win!", 340, 160, the entry "ink" of palette
    set the text size to 26
    etch words with "[points] points", 400, 240, the entry "ink" of palette
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  open a world with "Hop!", 960, 540
  choose the colours
  build the level
  fingerprint the level with platforms as saved text
  load the record
  start again
  set facing to 1
  set lives to 3
  set flying to the command fly
  set layers to a list containing (the command etch the sky, the command etch the level, the command etch the dangers, the command etch the player, the command etch the score)
  every frame:
    if not won:
      run and jump
      move across
      move up and down
      pick up coins
      if player y exceeds 700 or the danger touching is something: lose a life
      if score is the size of coins and player x exceeds 3030: set won to yes
      set seconds to seconds plus frame time
    if on ground and (speed x exceeds 3 or speed x falls below -3): leave with (dust, (player x plus 15) horizontal (player y plus 38) vertical)
    otherwise if the size of the items of dust exceeds 0: remove item 1 from the items of dust
    for each n from 1 to the size of bees:
      set item n of bees to invoke flying with (item n of bees, ticks)
    fly with (queen, ticks)
    set camera to clamp (player x minus 360) between 0 and 2240
    set ticks to ticks plus frame time
    for each layer in layers: invoke layer
  whenever won:
    set points to round (3000 times 0.97 to the power seconds) plus score times 100
    meanwhile save the record with (seconds, points)
  every 0.5 seconds:
    set blink to not blink
and the universe said i love you
